From c0a9078220714b0cb2214cec9a6a27fa6575c8d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): phantom-ref scan resolves short-form
 ids by prefix and skips ids inside paths/branches

The completion-summary advisory (`suspected_hallucinated_references`) extracted `t_<8+hex>` tokens and looked them
up by exact id, so a card's own 8-hex prefix (worker-4: t_01a1cf03b74efb8d flagged `t_01a1cf03` from its branch
`design/t_01a1cf03-land-lane`) counted as phantom.

- `_TASK_ID_PROSE_RE` gains the `(?<![\w/])` lookbehind `kanban_block_policy._TASK_ID` uses: a token embedded in a
  path, branch or identifier is not a reference.
- A token shorter than a full id (`t_` + 16 hex) resolves when any task id starts with it: local board, Board
  replicas (`replica_prefixes`) and the hub replica (`hub_replica_lookup`). Full ids keep the exact lookup.
- The scan moves to `hermes_cli/kanban_prose_refs.py` (kanban_db re-exports it) to keep kanban_db.py under its cap.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_false_signals.py (branch-embedded prefix, prose prefix, ghost full id,
orphan prefix, hub-replica prefix) and test_kanban_board_replica_refs.py (Board-replica prefix).
